# Next.js App Router standards (web-portal)

Paths below are relative to `apps/web-portal/` (no `src/` prefix). Shared HTTP/DTO types come from `@cloudpulse/api-contracts`; feature `types/` are view-models and adapters on top. Playwright is a sibling Nx app at `apps/web-portal-e2e` (`{app}-e2e` suffix, not `e2e-{app}`).

Prefer App Router server-first patterns over client-side SPA patterns.

MUST is React / Next.js. PREFER is the CloudPulse enterprise default: one library, every time. Do not add a second pattern.

## Hard constraints

- Server Components by default. `'use client'` only on interactive leaves.
- Do not put `'use client'` on `page.tsx` or `layout.tsx`.
- `app/` is routing only. Domain logic lives in `features/<name>/`.
- Do not pass raw DB or API entities to client components; use adapters.

## Directory layout

```text
apps/web-portal/
├── app/                      # routing primitives only
│   ├── (auth)/               # route groups
│   ├── dashboard/
│   │   ├── page.tsx          # thin entry: fetch via RSC, render features
│   │   ├── layout.tsx
│   │   └── loading.tsx
│   ├── api/                  # webhooks or public REST only
│   └── global.css            # only unscoped global styles
├── components/ui/            # design-system primitives (shadcn)
├── lib/                      # shared infrastructure (db, redis, auth, env)
└── features/
    └── <feature-name>/       # e.g. billing, users, inventory
        ├── components/       # presenters and client UI
        ├── actions/          # Server Actions (mutations)
        ├── queries/          # RSC data-fetching (DB/ORM)
        ├── schemas/          # Zod schemas
        ├── types/            # domain and view-model types
        ├── utils/            # pure domain logic and adapters
        └── tests/            # colocated unit and component tests
```

## 1. Domain architecture

Organize by domain feature, not by framework artifact type.

- MUST keep `app/` thin: read search/route params, call feature queries, pass minimal props.
- MUST NOT put business logic, queries, or large component trees in `app/` routes.
- MUST import shared UI from `components/ui/` and infra from `lib/` only.
- MUST NOT import another feature's private files. Cross-feature use goes through that feature's `index.ts`.

## 2. RSC vs client

RSCs are containers; client components are leaf presenters.

- MUST default to Server Components (`async function Feature()`).
- MUST use RSCs for DB/ORM, auth, headers, and cookies.
- MUST add `'use client'` only for event handlers, browser APIs, or local UI state (`useState`, `useReducer`, animations).
- MUST NOT put `'use client'` on `page.tsx` or `layout.tsx`. Isolate interactivity in a child.
- MUST add `import 'server-only'` at the top of `queries/`, `lib/db/`, and other server-only utilities.

```tsx
// BAD — client wrapper on a route
'use client';
export default function Page() {
  return <BillingDashboard />;
}

// GOOD — server route, client leaf
export default async function Page() {
  const summary = await getBillingSummary();
  return <BillingDashboard summary={toBillingSummaryView(summary)} />;
}
```

## 3. Serialization and adapters

- MUST NOT pass raw database entities (Prisma, Drizzle rows) or raw API entities across the RSC-to-client boundary.
- MUST reshape data in `features/<feature>/utils/*.adapters.ts` before client props.
- MUST pass only the primitive fields the client component needs to render.

```ts
// BAD
<InvoiceRow invoice={prismaInvoice} />

// GOOD
<InvoiceRow view={toInvoiceRowView(prismaInvoice)} />
```

## 4. Files and exports

- MUST put one exported component per file.
- MUST NOT colocate private helpers, formatters, or adapters inside a component file. Extract them to `features/<feature>/utils/`, export them, and unit-test them in isolation.
- MUST use named function exports for domain components, actions, and utilities: `export function FeatureCard() {}`.
- MUST use `export default` only for App Router files: `page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`.
- MUST colocate extra component types in `<component-name>.types.ts`; feature-wide types in `features/<feature>/types/`.
- MUST style with Tailwind or a colocated `<component-name>.module.css`.
- MUST NOT add unscoped global CSS outside `app/global.css`.

## 5. State

- MUST treat server data as RSC + Suspense + Server Action revalidation (`revalidatePath`, `revalidateTag`).
- MUST NOT copy server data into client `useState` or `useEffect`.
- MUST keep shareable state in the URL: filters, tabs, sort, search, pagination.
- PREFER nuqs as the only API for that URL state. Do not mix ad-hoc `useSearchParams` / stringly-typed query parsing.
- PREFER Zustand as the only store for shared client UI (drawers, wizards, disconnected leaves). Do not add React Context stores or extra state libraries. Stores stay client-only; do not put server data in them.

## 6. Validation and mutations

- MUST validate route params, search params, API bodies, and Server Action payloads with Zod.
- MUST infer types from schemas (`z.infer<>`).
- MUST put mutations in `features/<feature>/actions/` with `'use server'`. Parse input, check auth, and return a typed error inside the action — treat it as a public endpoint.
- PREFER next-safe-action as the only wrapper around those actions. Do not invent a second action helper.
- MUST submit forms through Server Actions.
- PREFER React Hook Form + `@hookform/resolvers/zod` as the only form library. Do not use `useActionState` or other form kits. The component handles UI feedback; submit still goes to a Server Action.

```ts
export const updateUserSchema = z.object({
  id: z.string().uuid(),
  name: z.string().min(1),
});
export type UpdateUserInput = z.infer<typeof updateUserSchema>;
```

## 7. Vitest

- MUST colocate unit/integration tests in `features/<feature>/tests/` as `*.test.ts` or `*.test.tsx`.
- MUST export every util, adapter, and calculation in `features/<feature>/utils/` and give each an isolated unit test (no DOM). Target ≥95% coverage on `utils/`.
- MUST test client presenters by behavior (visible output on click), not internal state.
- MUST query with `getByRole` / `getByLabelText`, not test IDs or CSS classes.
- MUST NOT render RSCs in Vitest. Unit-test queries as async functions against a mocked data layer; pass mock view-models into client presenters.
- MUST prefer dependency injection over `vi.mock()`.

## 8. Playwright

Nx convention: e2e is its own application, named with an `-e2e` suffix, sibling to the app under `apps/`.

- MUST put journeys in `apps/web-portal-e2e/` (project name `web-portal-e2e`). Example: `apps/web-portal-e2e/src/auth.spec.ts`.
- MUST run with `nx e2e web-portal-e2e`.
- MUST NOT use a repo-root `e2e/` folder or an `e2e-web-portal` prefix.
- MUST locate with `getByRole`, `getByLabel`, `getByText`. Use `getByTestId` only when semantic HTML cannot distinguish the control.
- MUST run against `next build` + `next start` (not only `next dev`).
- MUST NOT use `page.waitForTimeout()`. Await `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` or network idle.
- MUST reuse authenticated `storageState` instead of logging in through the UI every suite.
